Thank you for sharing, Peyman. I made this to help me study and understand research papers, and I hope others will find it helpful as well.

@docmilanfar: "I really enjoyed the explainer for our recent paper on 'Geometry of Noise' arXiv:2602.18428."

The linked explainers include one from intuitivepapers.ai that provides an interactive overview of the paper, focusing on intuition, figures, and verification against primary literature. It helps clarify why noise-blind diffusion models still generate outputs and which types tend to collapse.
